\title{misclassifyr: Estimation and Inference for Models of Misclassification}
\description{
Maximum likelihood estimation and inference for models of misclassification, in which a discrete latent outcome is observed only through two noisy measures, as described in Mattheis (2024). The package supplies tabulation helpers, a menu of parametric and non-parametric models for the misclassification distribution, delta-method standard errors and Monte Carlo confidence sets for a downstream regression coefficient, and a fast expectation-maximization estimator for the record-linkage model when the outcome has thousands of categories.
